Each whale has 40 gallons of blood. A shark has three times as much blood as a whale, so:

$$
40 \text{ gallons} \times 3 = 120 \text{ gallons per shark}
$$

For ten sharks:

$$
120 \text{ gallons} \times 10 = 1200 \text{ gallons}
$$

The total number of gallons of blood that ten sharks have is **1200**.

\boxed{1200}
